# Who must review what. Replace the placeholders with GitHub users or teams
# (for example @acme/ba-team). /dirox-project:protect-repo makes GitHub require their review on main.
# The last matching line wins. One owner's approval satisfies a line. GitHub never counts a PR author's
# own approval: on a two-person project, name both people on every line, so each can approve the other's PR.
# Behaviour (openspec/) has no owner here: the design gate covers large changes
# (.github/design-reviewers), and the code reviewer reads a normal change's specs.
# The rest of okf/ (the log, data, integrations, runbooks) is reviewed by the code reviewer.

# Knowledge: domain terms belong to whoever defines what to build, decisions and architecture to whoever
# designs the system.
/okf/domain/               @ledvincent
/okf/decisions/            @ledvincent
/okf/architecture/         @ledvincent

# The workflow itself: whoever sets up the project.
/.claude/                  @ledvincent
/.github/                  @ledvincent
